+- finding-source · {"version":1,"source":"inv-cc29fc83-52dd-468a-b12b-83f078e3ee3f/cluster-12","artifact":"reviews/inv-cc29fc83-52dd-468a-b12b-83f078e3ee3f/final-review-inv-cc29fc83-52dd-468a-b12b-83f078e3ee3f.cluster-12.md","kind":"final-review","verdict":"not ready (seat resurrect counts purge tombstones as revivable clones, so resurrecting a seat whose only clone was purged commits an active seat with no clone)","occurrences":[{"section":"Findings","position":1,"key":"`SeatResurrect` (plan and mutate) and the teamspace-resurrect plan do not filter out tombstones, although `do_resurrect_seat` does. This contradicts spec section 13 (\"A Finalize tombstone is not planned, ... resurrected\").","text":"`SeatResurrect` (plan and mutate) and the teamspace-resurrect plan do not filter out tombstones, although `do_resurrect_seat` does. This contradicts spec section 13 (\"A Finalize tombstone is not planned, ... resurrected\").\n  - At head, src/plan/core_kinds.rs: the `revived` loop in `SeatResurrect::plan` (around line 1576) and `revives_clone` in `SeatResurrect::mutate` (around line 1606) test only `lifecycle == Retired && retired_with(..)`. The same applies to the teamspace-resurrect plan loop around line 827.\n  - Effect: when the purged clone was the seat's only clone retired with it, `seat resurrect --active` previews a `clone.resurrect` and an `open_pane` for the tombstone. It then skips the \"create a fresh clone\" branch. `do_resurrect_seat` correctly skips the tombstone, so the commit leaves an active seat with no active clone. This was reproduced by the probe above.\n  - The cluster's own test `seat_resurrect_skips_a_purged_clone` does not catch this, because a live sibling is always revived."},{"section":"Findings","position":2,"key":"Name resolution includes tombstones. `grammar::resolve_clone(.., Scope::Retired)` matches tombstones by name. So `clone purge <name>`, run after a same-named clone was purged and a new one retired, fails as ambiguous and lists the inert tombstone as a candidate. Separately, an ambiguous retired-name match falls through to the live lookup, so with a live clone of the same name the operator gets \"retire it first\" instead of the ambiguity. Both cases only refuse; the id form works.","text":"Name resolution includes tombstones. `grammar::resolve_clone(.., Scope::Retired)` matches tombstones by name. So `clone purge <name>`, run after a same-named clone was purged and a new one retired, fails as ambiguous and lists the inert tombstone as a candidate. Separately, an ambiguous retired-name match falls through to the live lookup, so with a live clone of the same name the operator gets \"retire it first\" instead of the ambiguity. Both cases only refuse; the id form works."},{"section":"Findings","position":3,"key":"Before D2, purge of every seated clone writes a `Finalize{seat}` tombstone. Spec section 8 says \"A clone whose seat is already final (every seat before D2) is purged at once, with no intent\", but 14.2 (\"after D2\"), which supersedes it, together with hg-66u.35's description, prescribes the tombstone always. No finalize want exists until hg-66u.31 (D2-gated, open), so these tombstones persist until then. 14.2 makes a read showing the seat final count as acknowledgement, so they will drain once that want lands. They are inert meanwhile: excluded from status, resurrect, undo, and the one-live-clone-per-seat check.","text":"Before D2, purge of every seated clone writes a `Finalize{seat}` tombstone. Spec section 8 says \"A clone whose seat is already final (every seat before D2) is purged at once, with no intent\", but 14.2 (\"after D2\"), which supersedes it, together with hg-66u.35's description, prescribes the tombstone always. No finalize want exists until hg-66u.31 (D2-gated, open), so these tombstones persist until then. 14.2 makes a read showing the seat final count as acknowledgement, so they will drain once that want lands. They are inert meanwhile: excluded from status, resurrect, undo, and the one-live-clone-per-seat check."},{"section":"Findings","position":4,"key":"The `ReleaseKey` branch cannot be reached at head. Both call sites pass `reservation = None` with the comment \"hg-66u.13 passes the recorded key reservation\", but hg-66u.13 is closed and that work was split into hg-66u.43 (open, D1-gated), so the comment points at the wrong bead. No CloneRecord reservation field exists yet, so this is expected gate-ordering, not a defect.","text":"The `ReleaseKey` branch cannot be reached at head. Both call sites pass `reservation = None` with the comment \"hg-66u.13 passes the recorded key reservation\", but hg-66u.13 is closed and that work was split into hg-66u.43 (open, D1-gated), so the comment points at the wrong bead. No CloneRecord reservation field exists yet, so this is expected gate-ordering, not a defect."},{"section":"Must fix before landing","position":1,"key":"SeatResurrect::plan/mutate (revived and revives_clone) and the teamspace-resurrect plan loop in src/plan/core_kinds.rs must skip `is_tombstone()` clones like do_resurrect_seat does; reproduced: retire a seat whose only clone is seated, purge that clone, then `seat resurrect --active` commits an Active seat with zero active clones and previews clone.resurrect/open_pane for the tombstone; add a regression test without a live sibling.","text":"SeatResurrect::plan/mutate (revived and revives_clone) and the teamspace-resurrect plan loop in src/plan/core_kinds.rs must skip `is_tombstone()` clones like do_resurrect_seat does; reproduced: retire a seat whose only clone is seated, purge that clone, then `seat resurrect --active` commits an Active seat with zero active clones and previews clone.resurrect/open_pane for the tombstone; add a regression test without a live sibling."},{"section":"Untested scope","position":1,"key":"seat resurrect --active of a seat whose only retired clone is a purge tombstone (the existing test always has a reviving sibling).","text":"seat resurrect --active of a seat whose only retired clone is a purge tombstone (the existing test always has a reviving sibling)."},{"section":"Untested scope","position":2,"key":"teamspace resurrect preview over a seat holding a purge tombstone.","text":"teamspace resurrect preview over a seat holding a purge tombstone."},{"section":"Untested scope","position":3,"key":"clone purge by name when a same-named tombstone, or a second retired clone of the same name, exists.","text":"clone purge by name when a same-named tombstone, or a second retired clone of the same name, exists."},{"section":"Untested scope","position":4,"key":"clone purge plan/apply race: a clone un-retired or purged between plan and confirm (relied_on rev guard is present but not exercised by a test).","text":"clone purge plan/apply race: a clone un-retired or purged between plan and confirm (relied_on rev guard is present but not exercised by a test)."},{"section":"Untested scope","position":5,"key":"ReleaseKey tombstone path (unreachable until hg-66u.43 records a reservation).","text":"ReleaseKey tombstone path (unreachable until hg-66u.43 records a reservation)."},{"section":"Deferred OK","position":1,"key":"Before D2, purge writes Finalize tombstones that persist until the hg-66u.31 finalize want exists; they are inert and are drained by the final-read acknowledgement of spec 14.2.","text":"Before D2, purge writes Finalize tombstones that persist until the hg-66u.31 finalize want exists; they are inert and are drained by the final-read acknowledgement of spec 14.2."},{"section":"Deferred OK","position":2,"key":"Name resolution for `clone purge <name>` should exclude tombstones and not let a retired-name ambiguity fall through to the live lookup; refusal-only, the id form works.","text":"Name resolution for `clone purge <name>` should exclude tombstones and not let a retired-name ambiguity fall through to the live lookup; refusal-only, the id form works."},{"section":"Deferred OK","position":3,"key":"Stale b