+- finding-source · {"version":1,"source":"inv-cc29fc83-52dd-468a-b12b-83f078e3ee3f/cluster-16","artifact":"reviews/inv-cc29fc83-52dd-468a-b12b-83f078e3ee3f/final-review-inv-cc29fc83-52dd-468a-b12b-83f078e3ee3f.cluster-16.md","kind":"final-review","verdict":"not ready (no production producer admits ThreadsSeatAssignment or writes a Restore intent, participation is still occupant-keyed, and pre-D2 purge writes a Finalize tombstone nothing will remove)","occurrences":[{"section":"Concerns","position":1,"key":"Assign does not check the target clone's lifecycle: a late resolve acknowledgement after the clone retired (or after purge left a ReleaseKey tombstone) writes `threads_seat` onto a retired clone or an \"inert\" tombstone (§13), since `check_free` only inspects other clones and `rec.lifecycle`/`is_tombstone()` are never consulted for `rec` itself (src/threads/assignment.rs Assign arm).","text":"Assign does not check the target clone's lifecycle: a late resolve acknowledgement after the clone retired (or after purge left a ReleaseKey tombstone) writes `threads_seat` onto a retired clone or an \"inert\" tombstone (§13), since `check_free` only inspects other clones and `rec.lifecycle`/`is_tombstone()` are never consulted for `rec` itself (src/threads/assignment.rs Assign arm)."},{"section":"Concerns","position":2,"key":"The one-live-clone-per-seat invariant is enforced only on Assign/Succeed, not on other commits: with A on seat-a retired, B may be assigned seat-a (test `threads_seat_assign_rejects_a_seat_another_live_clone_holds` shows exactly this), and a later undo of A's retirement re-activates A with `threads_seat = seat-a` without any check, giving two non-retired clones on one seat; §2 calls for a writer validator.","text":"The one-live-clone-per-seat invariant is enforced only on Assign/Succeed, not on other commits: with A on seat-a retired, B may be assigned seat-a (test `threads_seat_assign_rejects_a_seat_another_live_clone_holds` shows exactly this), and a later undo of A's retirement re-activates A with `threads_seat = seat-a` without any check, giving two non-retired clones on one seat; §2 calls for a writer validator."},{"section":"Concerns","position":3,"key":"Succeed does not reject `seat == from`: it would push the current seat into history and mark `threads_done` without any actual succession.","text":"Succeed does not reject `seat == from`: it would push the current seat into history and mark `threads_done` without any actual succession."},{"section":"Must fix before landing","position":1,"key":"B1 undelivered: `bookkeeping.threads_seat` Assign has no production admitter at head (admit_threads_seat only in src/plan/tests.rs:3458 and src/undo/tests.rs:504; resolve-seat want hg-66u.7 absent), so no clone is ever bound to a threads seat.","text":"B1 undelivered: `bookkeeping.threads_seat` Assign has no production admitter at head (admit_threads_seat only in src/plan/tests.rs:3458 and src/undo/tests.rs:504; resolve-seat want hg-66u.7 absent), so no clone is ever bound to a threads seat."},{"section":"Must fix before landing","position":2,"key":"B7/B10 undelivered (pre-D2 interim, ungated): no undo/resurrection commit calls `write_restore_intent` and no executor admits Succeed/Acknowledge/MarkLaunched/ClearOnReattach, so graph undo cannot restore a closed clone onto its seat or its successor (hg-66u.29/.30/.32 open).","text":"B7/B10 undelivered (pre-D2 interim, ungated): no undo/resurrection commit calls `write_restore_intent` and no executor admits Succeed/Acknowledge/MarkLaunched/ClearOnReattach, so graph undo cannot restore a closed clone onto its seat or its successor (hg-66u.29/.30/.32 open)."},{"section":"Must fix before landing","position":3,"key":"B8 undelivered: src/threads/effects.rs `clone_wants` still keys desired/released invitations on the occupant; `occupancy_end_releases_requirement` and `clone_retirement_releases` pass at head, so agent exit and clone retirement still release memberships (hg-66u